## #02 — One JSON inspection contract
Implement `clerk.py show --store S --job ID --json [--instructions-base BASE]`.
Reuse the existing validated View/read/check path. Default human show output and
all mutation commands remain compatible. No app/bridge/kernel changes.
JSON schema identifier: clerk-handoff-inspection/1. Top-level fields:
schema, job_id, state, job, claim, returned, checks, problems.
- job: the validated queued job object (assignee, reviewer, instructions,
  expected_outputs, release and routed_by remain owned there), or null if unusable.
- claim: {by, token} from the validated claim, or null.
- returned: {by, delivery, evidence, artifacts} from the validated return, or null.
- checks: structured event/completion/artifact/instruction check results. Document
  exact enums/types; distinguish not checked/not applicable from verified good.
- problems: explicit typed diagnostics or strings, documented consistently.
State must distinguish queued/claimed/returned from unknown/incomplete/corrupt;
an invalid structure never produces a successful clean returned object. Do not
present unverified fields as usable. Tokens and names remain labels, not auth.
For valid nonreturned phases, null returned is normal; don't invent outputs.
For missing/corrupt records or OS failures reached by show, emit valid JSON with
nonzero exit and diagnostics, no mixed human stdout or traceback. CLI syntax errors
may retain argparse's normal stderr/exit 2 behavior. Inspection never writes.

## #03 — Tests and demonstration
In external disposable stores/copies, cover queued, claimed, resumed, returned,
identical resend, changed artifact, unusable instructions, unknown job, partial or
missing witness/event and expected read errors. Parse JSON in a fresh process;
check exact actor/reviewer/output set, claim token, returned delivery and artifact
hashes against the actual recorded source. Assert every store byte/name unchanged
before/after inspection, including on failure. Do not silently regenerate views.
Keep existing human CLI tests and 28-test suite/demonstration passing with skips
reported. No new network/model calls, timers or broad fuzzing. A JSON shape is
not an approval/acceptance record. No duplicated editable job state or database.

